er of the xp  protein expression systems  to produce recombinant antigens for the  development of vaccines and serological  tests  so let me start with what is protein  expression now naturally i'm sure that  you're all very much aware of what  protein expression is  but i think this serves as a good  reminder that cells are factories  and in protein expression we are simply  exploiting a cell's ability  to produce protein and re-tasking it to  produce our desired protein of interest  which in this case will be the various  coronavirus antigens  that will have been genetically encoded  into an expression construct  the efficiency of the protein expression  system will ultimately determine  both the yield and the quality of the  expressed  proteins so if we put this into the  vaccine researcher  what are the needs with regard to regard  to recombinant protein expression  systems  well certainly the expression system  must have the ability to  produce vaccine candidates rapidly  certainly during the exploratory phase  of vaccine development we need to be  able to produce and  uh evaluate numerous candidates  and then we as we progress them we would  like to shorten the time  to clinic equally we need to be able to  produce higher yield of protein  again during the exploratory phases  we're after high yield because typically  we're working with low culture volumes  and so we need to make  functional assessments of the proteins  being produced  having pre-generated our candidate  vaccines one then needs to be able to  scale manufacturing  quickly and cost effectively  so here's an overview of the vaccine  development workflow  you can see the exploratory phases the  developmental phases and the  manufacturing phases here  over on the left-hand ci side we see  pathogen identification  followed by a candidate vaccine panels  which will have been generated based on  sequence information from the virus  itself  having screened panels of candidate  vaccines and selected appropriate  candidates for further development  frequently groups will then go on to  make a stable expression cell lines from  those candidates  the stable cell lines will be further  evaluated and eventually  used in pilot scale manufacturing for  potential clinical  evaluation assuming that clinical  evaluation is successful  after various rounds of evaluation the  candidate will be moved into large-scale  manufacturing  so where do our xp systems fit into this  workflow  well certainly our xp transient  expression systems  fit very nicely into the screening of  candidate vaccine panels  but you will also see later in this  presentation  that we now offer you a path with the xp  systems through to  from transient expression through to  trade a stable cell line generation  makes these xp systems unique  um these xp systems are complete systems  they are fully optimized systems uh each  component in the system has been  optimized individually and both as a  system using design of experimentation  approaches  each system comprises cells  and these cells have been selected for  their high specific protein productivity  in all cases they are grown as single  cell spensions  so cell suspensions at very high cell  densities  the media systems are all chemically  defined animal origin free  and manufactured under cgmp principles  each system has its own unique  transfection reagent  we need to achieve high transfection  efficiency at high cell density  and so we've had to develop new  transfection reagents for that purpose  the systems are also provided with  expression enhancers and feeds to  further boost expression  and of course we can also provide  expression vectors of which we have a a  whole family of vectors that can be used  for  uh expression in the xbxp systems  interestingly each xp system is also  provided with what we call a technical  control  so that you can ensure that the systems  are functioning optimally in your  laboratory  prior to actually introducing vaccine  candidates into the expression system  that i would now like to take a look at  some of the exp  xp systems that are available to you and  the first system i would like to  describe  is the so-called xb293 expression system  which is a mammalian cell-based  expression system  that uses a heck 293 cell line  now this system enables the rapid  development of vaccine candidates  and generates high yields of protein  typically in the system we have seen up  to one gram per liter  of protein being produced in transient  transfection  and again this is an integrated system  meaning that all of the components of  the system have been individually  optimized  as well as the system itself the  components of the system are the xb293f  cells which have been adapted to high  density suspension culture  the chemically defined expression medium  which is transfection compatible as well  as the unique transfection reagent used  to transfect your constructs of interest  into the high-density cell lines  hotel cultures  the second x i would like to describe to  you briefly  is the xp cho expression system  this is also a mammalian expression  system that uses a cho  s cell background for expression this  system provides a high yield  end-to-end platform enabling a faster  time  to clinic when used in transient mode  we see yields of protein up to three  grams per liter in the system  it's also imp importantly that this  system uh provides you  with just one cell line that you can use  all the way from  discovery through to the the clinic  this means that your exploratory work  can be done using our research use only  exp cho s cell line  exploring vaccine candidates but as you  progress them through to development and  eventually through to manufacturing  you can work with our cgmp banked cell  line  either in transient mode or to produce  stable cell lines  for more clinically relevant work and of  course this is very important being able  to use the same cell line throughout the  development process because it enables  you to maintain protein quality  and function throughout the entire  workflow process  the xp chose system similar to the 293 f  system  comprises the cells which have been  again adapted to high density cell  suspension culture  the chemically defined animal origin  free expression medium  the novel transfection reagent that  allows transfection of these high  density cell cultures  a technical control this is the antibody  expressing positive control  again enabling optimization of the  system in your lab  prior to actually expressing your own  constructs the optipro  serum free medium for complexing  the dna vectors that will be transfected  into the cell  background as well as exp cho stable  production media  which is a media formulation that's been  developed specifically should you decide  to take  your constructs into stable cell lines  so i'd really like to to just to  reinforce  um that there is an easy transition from  performing uh  transient work uh through to performing  stable work with the exp cho  system the on the left hand side you see  the complement of  xp cho transient tools  which are research use only but should  you decide to progress  candidates towards the clinic you can  switch to our cgmp banked  exp cho s cells along with our stable  production medium  which provides you a very nice  transition from exploratory work through  to development  and again through to the clinic and  again this is really the main benefit  here is that you can  maintain the quality and the function of  your protein  from early exploratory work through to  development and manufacturing  so in the next slide i've really  overlaid our vaccine development  workflow diagram that you saw previously  to show you where the exp cho systems  will be used so  and typically we're seeing that the exp  cho transient systems are being used in  the screening  of antigens these are the vaccine  candidates uh once candidates have been  selected for downstream progression  then groups will frequently switch to  our expicho  stable platform uh enabling stable cell  line generation in a cgmp bank cell line  clinical grade manufacturing of pilot  batches of vaccine for evaluation  and eventually through to large-scale  manufacturing  the third i would like to describe is  the xbsf  expression system this is an  insect based expression system that uses  the sf9 cell background  and it provides a cost-effective  solution for vaccine discovery  interestingly in head to head studies we  see that this system outperforms  all existing insect platforms with at  least three-fold higher yields of  protein  this is also uh the first insect  expression system that uses a chemically  defined medium  there are no yeast delayed presence in  in this medium and we also provide the  system with express enhancers to further  boost  expression by working with chemically  defined media of course we can ensure  that we have  consistent cell growth and consistent  protein expression yields  run after run the ability to actually  make  macular virus in a cell suspension  cultures  means that we have a very short times  from construct to protein  so there are no there is no requirement  for viral amplification  using the xbsf system which means that  we are  already generating protein from  constructs within six to ten days which  is approximately half that  of most other expression systems uh  insect expression systems  uh the components of this system  comprise again the xbsf9 cells which  have been adapted to  high density cell suspension culture the  chemically defined media  an enhancer a protein expression  enhancer a  transfection system for transfecting  back mids into the sf9 cells  the back-to-back expression system  the dh10 back competent cells  for generating the recombinant back mids  as well as the optimum reduced serum  medium  used for complexing dna prior to  transfection  the final part of this presentation i  would just like to introduce you briefly  to two case studies  the first here describes the work of dr  keith chapel  at the university of queensland in  australia dr  chapel is part of the coalition for  epidemic  preparedness innovations otherwise known  as sepi  and in their work following acquisition  of  viral sequence information from patient  samples  the the group have gone on to design  expression constructs using the  university of queensland's  so-called molecular clamping technology  which maintains the natural 3d structure  of the  expressed antigen throughout the work  the dr chapel has been performing  the xp cho system has been used as the  system of choice  because it provides fast high yields  and quality protein if you are  interested in  understanding more about the use of the  xp system in dr chapel's work  i'd like to refer you to the recent a  publication that's cited at the bottom  of this slide  in the second case study i'll be  describing briefly the work of dr jiang  zhu  at the ins at the scripps institute in  la jolla uh california  whose team are developing vaccines  against hiv this time  during the course of dr zoo's work  they've used extensively the xp  cho system to express native like  trimers and g  for 140 nanoparticles and they found  that the xp  cho system allowed them to improve both  the yield and the quality of the gp  140 nanoparticles if you're interested  in understanding more about the use of  the xp  cho system in dr zoo's work again i'd  like to refer you to the citation  at the bottom of this slide  i've introduced you to three xp  expression systems  firstly the xb293 transient expression  system which uses a heck 293  suspension cell line to provide high  yields of protein  up to one gram per liter secondly the  exp cho system which uses a cho  suspension line for transient expression  work  with yields of up to three grams per  liter but the system also provides a  path  through to the clinic through the  provision of a cgmp  banked cell line that can be used to  generate stables for development  and biomanufacturing work finally the  xbsf system for generating high yields  of protein from an insect cell line  maintained in a chemically defined yeast  elite free  medium for reproducible uh expression  performance  if you'd like to know more about any of  these systems then please refer to the  web  web link below or contact your local  firm official  representative thank you very much  thank you roland let's start the q a um  so how do the protein yields from the xp  cho expression system compare with from  freestyle cho  or the xp293 system  um thank you christy well working with  various test proteins  from different protein classes the exp  cho  expression system was found to yield  between 25  to 160 fold more protein than the  freestyle cho  expression system and we see between two  to four  fold more protein than the xb293  expression system and do i need to  change media after transfection  in the xv293 and xp chose systems  uh no you don't in fact so that was one  of the the design prerequisites of these  projects so the media systems  in both the xb293 and the xp cho system  have been designed to be transfection  compatible and there is no requirement  to change the media  uh post transfection can the xp systems  be used to express things that could  then be used in the clinic  the culture media and the transfection  reagents used in the xb293 and xp cho  systems and in fact as well as the xbsf  system  are all chemically defined animal origin  free  and all manufactured under cgmp  each of these systems is provided with a  cell line for  research use only however we also have  cgmp banked master banks for the xb 293  and the xp cho cell lines so for those  groups seeking to express protein for  downstream use in the clinic  we are able to provide a complete and  fully cgmp compliant expression system  along with the documentation that will  be required by the regulator  and how cost effective are the xp  systems for expressing proteins of  interest  well all three xp systems the xb293 xp  cho and xbsf  represent the highest yielding  expression systems available in the  market today  and would normally be expected to  provide you with the lowest cost  milligram of protein  that you have probably ever produced  how many days of culture acquired before  harvesting protein with the xpsf system  uh well depending on the particular  protein being expressed  the harvest time will typically between  day 6 and day 10 post transfection  harvest time is typically a parameter  that we would recommend should be  included as part of your expression  optimization  process as it can impact protein quality  we typically find that the whole process  of generating bachelor viral stocks  through to harvesting protein is roughly  half that of other bachelor viral  systems available today  and this is because we're able to  eliminate the need for viral  amplification steps  prior to initiating our expression runs  thereby significantly reducing the time  it takes  to generate protein from novel  constructs  and where can i find additional engine  on the xp systems  well for additional information i can  refer you to  thermofisher.com forward slash protein  expression in one word  otherwise please take contact with your  local thermo fisher representative  great thank you very much we'll wrap it  up there we'd like to panelist roland  leathers  and our sponsor thermo fisher scientific  thank you all for joining us for this  session  you

